# API Routes Reference

The frontend provides a comprehensive API for communication between the VS Code extension and the web interface.

## Authentication Endpoints

### GitHub Token Exchange
- **POST** `/api/auth/vscode/github-exchange` - [route.ts](mdc:pocket-agent/pocket-agent-frontend/src/app/api/auth/vscode/github-exchange/route.ts)
  - Exchanges GitHub OAuth tokens for service JWTs
  - Used by VS Code extension during authentication
  - Returns JWT token with 7-day expiration

## Chat Data Endpoints

### Chat Updates
- **POST** `/api/chat/update` - [route.ts](mdc:pocket-agent/pocket-agent-frontend/src/app/api/chat/update/route.ts)
  - Receives chat content updates from VS Code extension
  - Stores data in Redis with user-scoped keys
  - Requires JWT authentication

### Chat Listing
- **GET** `/api/chats/list` - [route.ts](mdc:pocket-agent/pocket-agent-frontend/src/app/api/chats/list/route.ts)
  - Returns list of active chat sessions for authenticated user
  - Used by web interface for tab navigation
  - Includes metadata: windowId, name, lastUpdated

### Individual Chat Content
- **GET** `/api/chat/[windowId]` - [route.ts](mdc:pocket-agent/pocket-agent-frontend/src/app/api/chat/[windowId]/route.ts)
  - Returns specific chat content by window ID
  - Includes HTML content, name, and last updated timestamp
  - User-scoped access (users can only see their own chats)

## Message Communication

### Send Message to Cursor
- **POST** `/api/message/send-to-cursor` - [route.ts](mdc:pocket-agent/pocket-agent-frontend/src/app/api/message/send-to-cursor/route.ts)
  - Queues messages to be sent to Cursor
  - Used by web interface message form
  - Stores commands in Redis for extension polling

### Command Polling
- **GET** `/api/commands/poll-outgoing/[windowId]` - [route.ts](mdc:pocket-agent/pocket-agent-frontend/src/app/api/commands/poll-outgoing/[windowId]/route.ts)
  - Polled by VS Code extension for pending commands
  - Returns queued messages for specific window
  - Removes messages from queue after retrieval

## Authentication Requirements

### Service Token (Extension)
- Required for: `/api/chat/update`, `/api/commands/poll-outgoing/[windowId]`
- Format: `Authorization: Bearer <jwt-token>`
- Token obtained via `/api/auth/vscode/github-exchange`

### Session Cookie (Web Interface)
- Required for: `/api/chats/list`, `/api/chat/[windowId]`, `/api/message/send-to-cursor`
- Managed automatically by Auth.js
- GitHub OAuth-based authentication

## Data Storage Keys

### Redis Key Patterns
```
user:{userId}:chats:list          # List of active chat IDs
user:{userId}:chat:{windowId}     # Individual chat content
user:{userId}:commands:{windowId} # Outgoing command queue
```

## Request/Response Formats

### Chat Update Request
```json
{
  "windowId": "string",
  "name": "string",
  "html": "string"
}
```

### Chat List Response
```json
[
  {
    "windowId": "string",
    "name": "string",
    "lastUpdated": "timestamp"
  }
]
```

### Send Message Request
```json
{
  "windowId": "string",
  "messageText": "string"
}
```

### Command Poll Response
```json
{
  "commands": [
    {
      "messageText": "string",
      "timestamp": "number"
    }
  ]
}
```

## Error Handling

### Common HTTP Status Codes
- **200**: Success
- **400**: Bad Request (missing/invalid parameters)
- **401**: Unauthorized (missing/invalid authentication)
- **404**: Not Found (chat not found or not accessible)
- **500**: Internal Server Error

### Error Response Format
```json
{
  "error": "Error message description"
}
```

## Rate Limiting & Performance

### Polling Intervals
- Chat list: 5 seconds
- Chat content: 3 seconds
- Command polling: Variable (controlled by extension)

### Caching Strategy
- Chat data cached in Redis with TTL
- No HTTP caching (real-time updates required)
- Efficient key-based lookups for user data

## Security Considerations

- All endpoints validate authentication tokens/sessions
- Redis keys are user-scoped to prevent data leakage
- CORS configured for development vs production
- JWT tokens expire after 7 days
- HTML content is stored as-is (sanitization on display)




